            <ArticleTitle>Hip pain in young adults: diagnosing femoroacetabular impingement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-45</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.JAA.0000470976.08461.91</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Symptomatic femoroacetabular impingement (FAI) predisposes patients to developing early osteoarthritis. This article reviews the criteria for diagnosing FAI, management strategies, and when to refer patients to an orthopedic provider for further evaluation and possible surgical intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
